WEBVTT

00:08.270 --> 00:11.120
He cracked the case?!

00:12.170 --> 00:14.330
This murder was a cold case...

00:14.330 --> 00:16.960
People said it would never be solved.

00:16.960 --> 00:20.870
That new student's unbelievable.
The greatest the school has ever seen!

00:20.870 --> 00:23.460
Does he understand how criminals think?

00:24.170 --> 00:28.670
Once you graduate, it could be the end
of unsolved cases around the world...

00:31.780 --> 00:33.440
Kamonohashi Ron!

00:34.100 --> 00:36.320
I'm flattered by your praise.

00:36.830 --> 00:41.350
Using such peerless abilities
to devote myself to becoming a detective

00:44.670 --> 00:46.290
is my life's calling.

00:59.040 --> 01:02.580
Ron    Kamonohashi's

00:59.040 --> 01:02.580
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

02:16.990 --> 02:20.950
<b>#02   The Case of the Locked-Room Piggy Bank Theft</b>

02:19.240 --> 02:20.950
<b>Building Manager</b>

02:20.950 --> 02:22.660
I wonder if he's home.

02:24.070 --> 02:25.830
Is it a locked room?! A suspicious death?!

02:29.800 --> 02:31.050
Ow...

02:31.050 --> 02:32.440
Heya, Toto.

02:33.510 --> 02:36.890
Kiku-san asked me to come check on you.

02:36.890 --> 02:38.180
I see you're alive and well.

02:38.180 --> 02:40.470
Did you think I'd been offed or something?

02:40.470 --> 02:43.480
So, have you brought me a case 
that will set my heart dancing?

02:48.050 --> 02:49.920
No. I haven't.

02:56.400 --> 02:58.280
The Floor of Indolence has taken him!

02:58.650 --> 03:00.280
Mumble, mumble, mumble, mumble...

03:00.550 --> 03:03.410
Huh? Stop mumbling and just speak up already.

03:03.410 --> 03:04.870
You're completely useless!

03:04.870 --> 03:07.330
Okay, I'd rather you
say that softer after all!

03:07.330 --> 03:10.890
You're wasting my overflowing passion
for solving mysteries

03:10.890 --> 03:13.800
and the greatest talent BLUE's ever seen.

03:14.150 --> 03:15.510
"Blue"?

03:16.470 --> 03:20.570
BLUE is the world's preeminent 
detective training academy.

03:20.570 --> 03:24.410
One hundred percent
of the best detectives are alumni.

03:24.410 --> 03:25.590
That'd be all of them!

03:26.590 --> 03:29.590
And of the lot, I had the top scores.

03:29.590 --> 03:32.860
They said I was the greatest 
genius to ever grace the school.

03:32.860 --> 03:35.390
What? That's incredible.

03:35.390 --> 03:36.450
But...

03:39.090 --> 03:43.020
during a practical exercise, 
all of the suspects I went after died,

03:43.020 --> 03:44.630
which put me under suspicion.

03:44.630 --> 03:49.990
I was expelled from BLUE and barred
from obtaining a detective's license.

03:51.540 --> 03:54.460
I'm forbidden even from sleuthing.

03:54.460 --> 03:56.280
What's a detective's license?

03:56.280 --> 04:00.020
The passport you need
to solve the toughest mysteries.

04:00.020 --> 04:04.050
Without it, I'm not permitted
access to any case.

04:04.050 --> 04:08.140
If I break the rules, 
BLUE will punish me with death.

04:08.140 --> 04:09.410
Death?!

04:10.350 --> 04:13.280
Wait... you were sleuthing
on that last case, weren't you?

04:13.280 --> 04:15.270
That was unavoidable.

04:15.270 --> 04:18.890
But from now on, on the surface,
you'll be doing the sleuthing,

04:18.890 --> 04:21.110
while I control you from behind the scenes.

04:21.110 --> 04:25.140
So <i>that's</i> why you said, "Starting today, 
you are a great detective!"

04:25.140 --> 04:26.650
You've got nothing better to do, right?

04:26.650 --> 04:30.330
No... but I don't like the sound
of being controlled.

04:30.330 --> 04:32.920
Sorry. Poor choice of words.

04:33.290 --> 04:34.890
You're my puppet.

04:34.890 --> 04:36.010
What are you, the devil?!

04:36.010 --> 04:37.580
Don't be so uptight.

04:37.580 --> 04:41.420
I'll conceal my identity, 
come with you to crime scenes,

04:41.420 --> 04:43.720
and give you instructions. That's all.

04:45.450 --> 04:48.230
So why not just give me
instructions over the phone?

04:48.230 --> 04:51.940
No. I want to pay my respects to the dead
and meet them for myself.

04:52.200 --> 04:54.980
<i>There he goes again, not listening...</i>

04:55.750 --> 04:57.300
I don't think that's happening.

04:57.300 --> 05:00.700
Yes, it is! As long as
 you're bringing me cases!

05:01.180 --> 05:03.240
<i>Talk about unreasonable!</i>

05:03.660 --> 05:09.140
Look, I'd love to be on a big case too,
but Amamiya-senpai decides the assignments.

05:09.140 --> 05:10.960
Amamiya-senpai?

05:13.030 --> 05:14.110
Hmm...

05:14.110 --> 05:15.680
She's beautiful, isn't she?

05:15.680 --> 05:17.880
I can see why she's got fans at the station.

05:19.600 --> 05:23.900
Since you're in this picture, 
you aren't the one who took it.

05:23.900 --> 05:28.720
The reason neither of you are looking 
at the camera is that it was taken in secret.

05:30.160 --> 05:31.620
You're right.

05:31.620 --> 05:35.250
A coworker who says he wants Amamiya-senpai
 to step on him sent it to me.

05:35.250 --> 05:36.530
He's got good taste.

05:36.530 --> 05:40.690
Unlike you, who gets shrill
every time you talk about her.

05:40.950 --> 05:43.360
That's because she's scary.

05:43.360 --> 05:44.660
Just today...

05:44.660 --> 05:46.370
<b>Investigation Division 1</b>

05:45.470 --> 05:46.370
Amamiya-san!

05:47.580 --> 05:49.790
A body was found on the riverbank!

05:49.790 --> 05:52.600
It's a male in his twenties 
with a head injury.

05:52.600 --> 05:54.500
They're sending a photo.

05:57.640 --> 05:59.750
This could have been foul play.

06:00.400 --> 06:01.420
We're heading to the scene!

06:01.700 --> 06:02.450
Yes, ma'am!

06:02.450 --> 06:03.880
Amamiya-senpai!

06:03.880 --> 06:05.320
Please take me too!

06:05.320 --> 06:08.470
No. I have much more fitting work for you.

06:08.470 --> 06:09.680
Here.

06:09.680 --> 06:10.560
Huh?

06:10.560 --> 06:11.430
What's this?

06:14.040 --> 06:17.150
Wha-bam!

06:17.150 --> 06:18.520
<b>Isshiki</b>

06:19.020 --> 06:20.530
Don't slack off, now.

06:20.530 --> 06:21.570
Ma'am!

06:23.830 --> 06:25.360
That's how it went.

06:25.360 --> 06:29.120
It's incredible that you have a file 
with work just for you, isn't it?

06:29.120 --> 06:33.070
Except they're all odd jobs 
or low-priority cases.

06:33.420 --> 06:35.330
People secretly call it the trash bin.

06:35.640 --> 06:37.670
One day, you'll have the last laugh.

06:39.200 --> 06:41.960
One day, the trash man will 
rule over all of humanity.

06:41.960 --> 06:43.720
I will not! You suck at being comforting!

06:43.720 --> 06:46.310
So, what's today's trash?

06:46.310 --> 06:47.180
Hey.

06:47.700 --> 06:51.070
There was a report about
missing money from a piggy bank.

06:51.070 --> 06:54.260
It ended up at Division 1
by some mistake or other.

06:54.260 --> 06:55.850
A piggy bank?

06:55.850 --> 06:59.590
It's what you might call 
an utterly impossible crime,

06:59.590 --> 07:03.160
but you don't seem like you'd be 
interested in the theft of small change.

07:12.530 --> 07:13.730
Let's go, Toto.

07:13.730 --> 07:15.000
I have so many questions!

07:15.000 --> 07:17.330
What is that? A-A disguise?

07:17.330 --> 07:18.710
What's gotten into you?

07:19.380 --> 07:22.290
Solving cases everyone else has abandoned...

07:22.290 --> 07:26.180
That duty falls to me,
the most talented man in BLUE's history.

07:26.180 --> 07:27.550
Now, let's go.

07:27.860 --> 07:29.390
H-Hey! Hang on!

07:30.350 --> 07:32.310
Whoa, that was close!

07:35.270 --> 07:36.280
Is it dead?

07:36.280 --> 07:37.410
It's sleeping.

07:43.230 --> 07:44.740
Yes?

07:45.230 --> 07:46.240
Oh.

07:46.240 --> 07:49.030
Hello. My name's Isshiki.
I'm with the police.

07:49.030 --> 07:52.200
And I'm Kanetamaru Kamoo
with Piggy Bank Emergency Services.

07:53.780 --> 07:55.910
P-Please, come in.

07:55.910 --> 07:57.740
Why do you sound like a money collector?

07:57.740 --> 07:59.430
Names and natures often agree, right?

07:59.430 --> 08:00.880
This one's on the nose!

08:00.880 --> 08:04.530
If you're found out, you're a dead man! 
Pick a normal name.

08:04.530 --> 08:05.090
Oh?

08:05.090 --> 08:06.300
What's this?

08:08.010 --> 08:10.220
This must be the piggy bank 
we've heard tell of.

08:10.220 --> 08:11.560
Kanetamaru!

08:11.560 --> 08:13.680
That's a suitcase.

08:13.680 --> 08:16.140
No wonder it's so large. Is it yours?

08:16.140 --> 08:18.160
It's my big sister's. 
She just returned home.

08:18.160 --> 08:20.650
It's just the two of you living here, right?

08:20.650 --> 08:22.830
And the lightened piggy bank would be...

08:22.830 --> 08:24.360
In the living room.

08:25.680 --> 08:28.280
Th-This is...

08:28.600 --> 08:30.910
This is the hit piggy bank 
with a rubber valve

08:30.910 --> 08:33.780
from which it is completely 
impossible to remove coins!

08:33.780 --> 08:35.490
The Impregnable Pig!

08:35.770 --> 08:37.350
How do you know all that?

08:37.350 --> 08:39.190
I just used your phone to look it up.

08:39.190 --> 08:40.460
Don't use it without asking!

08:40.460 --> 08:44.580
Pink was the popular color, 
but this one is yellow.

08:44.580 --> 08:45.670
That's right.

08:45.670 --> 08:48.410
It was all the local general store had left.

08:48.410 --> 08:49.650
And it was cheap, so...

08:49.650 --> 08:53.620
Now then, the day before yesterday, 
were both you and your sister out?

08:53.620 --> 08:58.460
Yes. I noticed it was lighter 
yesterday after I got home.

08:58.460 --> 09:00.400
Do you have any idea what happened?

09:00.400 --> 09:01.640
Well...

09:01.640 --> 09:02.940
Ow!

09:02.940 --> 09:04.650
My mustache got caught!

09:04.650 --> 09:05.860
When'd you grow that?!

09:05.860 --> 09:08.190
That's my sister's jewelry.

09:10.470 --> 09:12.870
Got one in your pocket 
and you gotta put it on, right?

09:12.870 --> 09:15.240
Wrong! Did you come 
just to get in the way?!

09:15.240 --> 09:18.390
Say, Toto, why do you think 
the thief didn't steal the jewelry?

09:18.390 --> 09:20.710
I see the question's written on your face.

09:20.710 --> 09:21.810
Huh?

09:21.810 --> 09:25.130
Wait, that's a good point. How weird.

09:25.130 --> 09:28.730
Speaking of weird, we've gotten 
a lot of silent phone calls lately.

09:28.730 --> 09:30.570
S-Silent phone calls?

09:30.570 --> 09:34.340
It's unsettling, so I made sure 
to lock up tight the day before yesterday.

09:35.800 --> 09:37.670
That makes the answer clear.

09:38.090 --> 09:39.670
Did you figure something out?

09:41.030 --> 09:42.050
I give up.

09:42.050 --> 09:43.190
What?!

09:43.190 --> 09:46.420
An impregnable piggy bank in a locked house...

09:46.420 --> 09:50.150
Pilfering money from there
 is truly an utterly impossible crime.

09:50.650 --> 09:53.830
Didn't you say solving
overlooked cases was your duty?

09:53.830 --> 09:56.770
Hang on. A-Are you drinking 
undiluted black sugar syrup?

09:54.100 --> 09:57.060
<b>Black Sugar Syrup</b>

09:54.100 --> 09:57.060
<b>The Most Delicious</b>

09:57.820 --> 09:59.460
I'm home!

09:59.460 --> 10:00.790
That's my sister!

10:05.010 --> 10:08.960
The day before yesterday, I was helping
 our parents and stayed at their house.

10:08.960 --> 10:11.330
I came back yesterday.

10:11.330 --> 10:14.090
And when my little sister got home...

10:14.090 --> 10:18.230
I noticed it was lighter when I picked it up
 to put some change in.

10:18.230 --> 10:21.680
I think she's just imagining it, but...

10:21.680 --> 10:23.270
Imagining it?

10:23.550 --> 10:27.480
<i>No new information, huh? This is a problem.</i>

10:27.480 --> 10:30.440
Why not leave it at that? 
Just a trick of the mind.

10:30.440 --> 10:32.580
Hey, don't toss the whole investigation!

10:32.580 --> 10:34.160
I'm not imagining things!

10:34.160 --> 10:37.660
This pig was as heavy as an iron statue!

10:45.070 --> 10:46.830
Nice, younger sister.

10:47.670 --> 10:49.540
That's what I wanted to hear.

10:50.830 --> 10:51.800
What?

10:51.800 --> 10:54.600
If that's case, let's break the piggy bank.

10:54.600 --> 10:56.010
Your Japanese isn't making sense!

10:56.010 --> 10:58.530
I don't mind, but...

10:58.530 --> 10:59.470
All right.

11:04.140 --> 11:06.570
I still think there's less than before.

11:06.570 --> 11:08.610
But there's no way to be certain.

11:09.040 --> 11:10.820
Whoa there. Please don't touch those.

11:11.530 --> 11:15.030
Toto is going to send them
to forensics for fingerprinting.

11:15.030 --> 11:17.880
I'm going for a walk, so let's meet up later.

11:18.500 --> 11:19.590
What?!

11:24.420 --> 11:25.710
There you are!

11:28.380 --> 11:29.630
You're late, Toto.

11:29.630 --> 11:31.340
I ran all the way here!

11:31.340 --> 11:33.880
Why are we out here anyway?

11:36.790 --> 11:38.570
Do we have the forensics results?

11:39.300 --> 11:43.230
Huh? The younger sister's fingerprints 
weren't on any of the coins?

11:43.230 --> 11:44.560
I knew it.

11:45.420 --> 11:47.020
You knew that?

11:51.260 --> 11:52.610
Is that...

11:54.400 --> 11:55.980
Amamiya-senpai!

11:59.550 --> 12:03.020
Amamiya-senpai! What are you doing here?

12:03.020 --> 12:04.730
Inspecting the corpse.

12:04.730 --> 12:07.080
I told you this morning not to come, didn't I?

12:07.080 --> 12:09.080
Is that the body there?

12:09.080 --> 12:11.550
Hey, wait! You can't just go in like...

12:11.550 --> 12:12.390
Who is that?

12:12.390 --> 12:14.810
H-He's a f-friend.

12:14.810 --> 12:16.130
Amamiya-kun.

12:16.900 --> 12:21.340
What if Isshiki Totomaru
solves this murder case?

12:22.480 --> 12:23.950
What kind of joke is that?

12:23.950 --> 12:27.650
Who knows? He's always such a prankster!

12:28.810 --> 12:33.540
If you screw this up and fail to put 
this expression on my face, you're fired, okay?

12:33.540 --> 12:34.520
Fired?!

12:41.240 --> 12:43.450
So, we finally meet.

12:43.760 --> 12:45.190
Who are you?!

12:45.910 --> 12:48.120
I will avenge you.

12:48.120 --> 12:50.660
Hey, what do you think you're doing?!

12:50.660 --> 12:52.340
Everything's in place.

12:52.340 --> 12:53.080
What?

12:55.470 --> 12:56.920
Detective Isshiki.

12:56.920 --> 12:57.760
Huh?

12:57.760 --> 12:59.470
You're up.

13:07.170 --> 13:09.680
Thank you for gathering here.

13:09.680 --> 13:12.810
First, I'd like to solve 
the mystery of the piggy bank.

13:12.810 --> 13:14.590
Skip that part.

13:14.590 --> 13:18.030
Petty cases like that have nothing
to do with Investigation Division 1.

13:18.030 --> 13:19.200
But...

13:19.200 --> 13:20.490
That's funny.

13:20.490 --> 13:24.070
I thought it was a case from 
Investigation Division 1's trash bin.

13:24.070 --> 13:25.280
What?

13:25.280 --> 13:28.690
U-Um, according to the forensics results,

13:28.690 --> 13:31.990
the coins in the piggy bank only have 
the older sister's prints on them.

13:31.990 --> 13:34.630
The younger sister's prints 
weren't on a single one.

13:34.630 --> 13:36.040
What?

13:36.040 --> 13:39.780
Does that mean that only the money 
my sister put in was stolen?

13:39.780 --> 13:43.010
But you can't open that piggy 
bank without breaking it.

13:43.010 --> 13:45.600
Something like that
would be impossible, right?

13:45.600 --> 13:47.840
Um, that's...

13:47.840 --> 13:50.750
Toto, I gave you a present 
from my walk, didn't I?

13:51.060 --> 13:53.110
Oh, th-that's right.

13:53.520 --> 13:56.610
If you're only thinking
about getting the coins out,

13:56.610 --> 13:58.280
then it does seem impossible.

13:58.750 --> 14:00.150
But if you can't get them out,

14:00.150 --> 14:03.950
you can always replace the whole bank
with a brand new one!

14:04.580 --> 14:06.380
That's our piggy bank!

14:06.380 --> 14:09.660
This same one is for sale
 at the local general store.

14:10.130 --> 14:13.250
There weren't fewer coins inside
 because they were stolen.

14:14.750 --> 14:18.100
The previous piggy bank was broken.
And in order to hide that,

14:18.530 --> 14:24.220
you purchased a replacement
and put other coins inside.

14:25.660 --> 14:27.240
Isn't that right...

14:28.960 --> 14:30.120
Miss?

14:32.470 --> 14:35.640
Wh-Why me?

14:35.640 --> 14:37.830
Why would I do something like that?

14:37.830 --> 14:41.690
If I broke it, then I wouldn't have 
to hide it. I could just tell her.

14:41.690 --> 14:43.860
W-Well...

14:43.860 --> 14:47.030
Your voice is cracking. Calm down, Toto.

14:49.700 --> 14:53.920
The reason you had to hide the fact that the 
piggy bank had been broken, no matter what,

14:53.920 --> 14:55.750
is here on this riverbank.

14:56.240 --> 14:57.590
It was a murder.

14:58.590 --> 15:00.920
The death of that man over there.

15:06.170 --> 15:11.140
When you came home, 
your stalker was lying in wait for you.

15:11.140 --> 15:12.840
Stalker?

15:12.840 --> 15:14.840
Oh, the silent phone calls!

15:15.690 --> 15:19.310
He chased you all the way
into the living room,

15:19.310 --> 15:22.390
and there was the piggy bank, 
as heavy as an iron statue.

15:22.390 --> 15:24.130
You struck and killed him with it.

15:29.890 --> 15:34.580
When you did, the piggy bank shattered, 
and blood got all over the coins.

15:35.160 --> 15:38.650
In order to conceal your crime, 
you bought a new one and tried

15:38.650 --> 15:40.440
to fill it with other coins.

15:40.800 --> 15:43.770
That's why only your prints are on them.

15:44.520 --> 15:46.580
Finally, you brought the body here.

15:47.150 --> 15:49.680
You used that suitcase 
in the entryway to move it.

15:54.070 --> 15:55.640
Given its size...

15:57.050 --> 15:59.800
it's far too large for just
an overnight stay with your parents.

16:00.360 --> 16:02.200
The mystery of the piggy bank...

16:02.200 --> 16:04.280
and the murder were connected?

16:05.690 --> 16:07.260
I managed to say everything.

16:13.260 --> 16:14.660
That can't be true...

16:16.930 --> 16:19.120
Right? It isn't true, right?

16:21.610 --> 16:22.790
Sis!

16:25.680 --> 16:27.260
It's just as he said.

16:28.680 --> 16:32.090
It... was all me.

16:41.820 --> 16:45.480
S-Still, if you consider how this started, 
it's the stalker's fault.

16:45.480 --> 16:48.190
Concealing a murder is a legitimate crime.

16:54.560 --> 16:55.830
Go drown.

16:56.320 --> 17:00.790
Someone who kills another and hides it 
has no right to live in this world.

17:00.790 --> 17:02.010
<i>This is bad!</i>

17:02.010 --> 17:04.000
<i>This is how he pressures criminals to death!</i>

17:04.600 --> 17:06.960
What is that? It's so cool...

17:08.000 --> 17:10.440
Miss! Don't pay any attention to him!

17:11.140 --> 17:14.100
He's just talking to himself! 
Don't take it seriously!

17:14.600 --> 17:16.060
Go drown.

17:20.920 --> 17:22.100
In the river.

17:23.640 --> 17:24.820
Yes...

17:26.210 --> 17:27.260
Sis!

17:27.260 --> 17:28.070
This is bad!

17:28.710 --> 17:31.530
Go drown. Go drown.

17:31.790 --> 17:33.300
Amamiya-senpai!

17:35.450 --> 17:38.390
Not so fast!

17:46.510 --> 17:49.920
Go drown... Go drown...

18:16.450 --> 18:17.370
They're all right!

18:17.370 --> 18:18.660
Sis!

18:25.980 --> 18:27.550
What have I...

18:29.810 --> 18:32.040
I did it again. Pressured someone to...

18:36.270 --> 18:39.470
I'm so glad she's safe. Thank you...

18:39.750 --> 18:40.700
Toto.

18:43.940 --> 18:46.400
<b>Investigation Division 1</b>

18:44.680 --> 18:46.400
Case closed.

18:46.830 --> 18:51.440
They found fragments of the piggy bank 
in the stalker's hair.

18:51.790 --> 18:54.590
His blood and prints were also at the house.

18:54.590 --> 18:57.120
It's all consistent with her confession.

18:57.930 --> 19:00.550
If they acknowledge she acted in self-defense,

19:00.550 --> 19:04.020
they may take that into consideration 
for her dumping his body as well.

19:04.770 --> 19:06.290
I hope they do.

19:08.110 --> 19:11.310
But the real problem here lies elsewhere!

19:11.310 --> 19:12.760
You two violated regulations!

19:13.100 --> 19:14.220
<i>Here it comes!</i>

19:14.220 --> 19:16.710
Entering a restricted area without permission!

19:16.710 --> 19:18.550
Interfering in an investigation!

19:18.550 --> 19:20.400
Intimidating a suspect!

19:20.400 --> 19:21.890
What's your friend's name?!

19:22.900 --> 19:25.820
I-It's Kamoo.

19:25.820 --> 19:27.540
Really?

19:30.060 --> 19:32.320
Kamoo-sama, huh?

19:32.320 --> 19:34.280
<i>Y-You gotta be kidding me.</i>

19:36.740 --> 19:37.210
<b>Building Manager</b>

19:37.630 --> 19:38.950
<b>Building Manager</b>

19:39.200 --> 19:41.640
I need to tell him how things turned out.

19:42.670 --> 19:44.410
Do you have a case 
that will set my heart dancing?!

19:46.560 --> 19:48.650
You just solved one yesterday!

19:49.350 --> 19:52.000
I was only joking, of course...

19:52.590 --> 19:54.800
Don't collapse into tears!

19:56.760 --> 19:58.760
<i>He really is an odd duck.</i>

19:59.180 --> 20:03.220
<i>He's totally weird. 
He's obsessed with cases. He's unreasonable.</i>

20:03.810 --> 20:07.030
<i>I never want to work with him again...</i>

20:07.030 --> 20:09.650
Amamiya-kun complimented 
you today, didn't she?

20:10.580 --> 20:13.190
Come to think of it,
she didn't have one kind word for me...

20:13.190 --> 20:15.410
Hold your head high, Toto.

20:15.410 --> 20:19.160
For a pure, naïve fool, 
you did incredibly good work.

20:19.160 --> 20:21.990
G-Gee, thanks.

20:23.120 --> 20:27.580
<i>Still, there's a part of me that's 
hoping for another difficult case...</i>

20:28.240 --> 20:33.040
<i>that's looking forward to Ron's deductions 
and the thrill of solving a mystery.</i>

20:33.310 --> 20:36.390
Well, this makes today a special occasion.

20:38.470 --> 20:39.910
A puppet was born!

20:39.910 --> 20:41.430
What'd you just say?!

20:46.790 --> 20:48.250
Principal,

20:48.250 --> 20:53.870
do you remember the man known 
as Kamonohashi Ron from class 87?

20:53.870 --> 20:56.520
Yes, of course I do.

20:55.070 --> 20:57.030
<b>BLUE's Principal
Emé Emmerich</b>

20:57.520 --> 21:02.200
The man with the highest marks 
in the history of BLUE?

20:58.740 --> 21:02.200
<b>Anatomy Instructor</b>

21:02.200 --> 21:03.400
That is correct.

21:02.200 --> 21:05.660
<b>Vice Principal</b>

21:03.400 --> 21:09.660
We've just received word from Japan. 
He's suspected of resuming detective work.

21:09.660 --> 21:11.120
Really?

21:11.120 --> 21:14.960
<b>Disguise Instructor</b>

21:11.120 --> 21:14.960
This may be the end of unsolved
cases as we know them in Japan.

21:15.360 --> 21:16.920
What are you saying?

21:16.920 --> 21:20.380
<b>Locked-Room Theory Instructor</b>

21:16.920 --> 21:21.880
Have you forgotten that all of the 
culprits in the case he handled died?

21:21.880 --> 21:26.060
He may give rise to yet another tragedy.

21:23.850 --> 21:26.810
<b>Timetable Instructor</b>

21:26.060 --> 21:27.300
Indeed.

21:27.560 --> 21:29.520
<b>Closed Circle Theory Instructor</b>

21:27.860 --> 21:29.520
I agree.

21:29.520 --> 21:33.210
Five years ago, we expelled him

21:33.210 --> 21:37.190
and barred him from obtaining
 a detective's license.

21:45.210 --> 21:47.290
The situation is clear.

21:47.600 --> 21:50.380
We at BLUE seek the truth.

21:50.380 --> 21:55.910
And to ensure that justice is never 
overshadowed by evil, we train detectives.

21:56.470 --> 21:59.720
We cannot have a detective who kills people.

22:00.720 --> 22:03.720
I order an investigation of Kamonohashi Ron.

22:06.470 --> 22:09.970
<b>Tracking Instructor</b>

22:06.470 --> 22:09.970
I believe I'm suited to the task.
